      "outcome_correct": true,
      "trace": "To find the value of \\(9 \\& 2\\) using the given operation definition \\(a \\& b = \\frac{\\sqrt{ab + a}}{\\sqrt{ab - b}}\\), we substitute \\(a = 9\\) and \\(b = 2\\).\n\nFirst, calculate the numerator:\n\\[ ab + a = 9 \\cdot 2 + 9 = 18 + 9 = 27 \\]\nSo, the square root of the numerator is:\n\\[ \\sqrt{27} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 3} = 3\\sqrt{3} \\]\n\nNext, calculate the denominator:\n\\[ ab - b = 9 \\cdot 2 - 2 = 18 - 2 = 16 \\]\nSo, the square root of the denominator is:\n\\[ \\sqrt{16} = 4 \\]\n\nNow, substitute these values back into the operation definition:\n\\[ 9 \\& 2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{27}}{\\sqrt{16}} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(9 \\& 2\\) is \\(\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{4}}\n\\]",
